Answer: Yes, the Central Bank of Nigeria (CBN) has issued public warnings specifically about the illegality of spraying Naira notes. As documented in a 2019 news report, the CBN's Director of Corporate Communications, Isaac Okorafor, reiterated this at an "interactive enlightenment session with stakeholders in Owerri," stating that under the CBN Act, abusing the Naira is an offence punishable by law, and "anyone caught in the act will either go to jail or pay the necessary fine."

